---
title: Thai crab fried rice
servings: 2
tags: [seafood, stir-fry, quick]
cuisine: thai
time: 23 minutes
source: Thai Crab Fried Rice (Khao Pad Pu) by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/crab-fried-rice-2
---

== Prik nam pla ==

Put the @Thai chiles{1}(thinly sliced) and @garlic{1%clove}(minced) in a small bowl. Cover with @fish sauce{1%tbsp} and add @lime juice{1%tsp}.

> The prik nam pla is optional and keeps for weeks in the fridge.

== Fried rice ==

Warm the @vegetable oil{3%tbsp} and @garlic{5-6%cloves}(chopped) in a #wok{} over medium heat until the smallest bits turn golden.

Add the @eggs{2}(large). Let them half set, then break them up so yolk and white stay marbled.

Turn the heat to high. Add the @jasmine rice{375%g}(cooked), @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @fish sauce{2%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp} and @ground white pepper{1/4%tsp}. Toss, pressing out any lumps.

Once the rice is evenly coloured, leave it ~{10-15%seconds} to toast, then toss. Repeat once or twice.

Add most of the @crab meat{4.6%oz}(fresh, not canned) and toss gently ~{30-60%seconds} to heat through.

Off the heat, toss in most of the @green onion{1}(chopped) and @?cilantro{}(chopped).

Plate and top with the rest of the crab and herbs. Serve with @cucumber{}(sliced), @lime wedges{} and the prik nam pla.
